cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this analysis plan or its code, please cite it as below.
title: >-
  The RESOLVE Swiss trial for people with chronic non-specific low back pain:
  statistical analysis plan for a cluster randomised controlled trial
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/jdegenfellner/Resolve_Swiss_Statistical_Analysis_Plan
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22655090
abstract: >-
  Statistical analysis plan for the RESOLVE Swiss cluster randomised controlled
  trial, together with the R code that reproduces every sample size, design
  effect and power figure reported in it. The practice is the unit of
  randomisation and the participant is the unit of analysis. The primary outcome
  is back-specific disability, measured with the Roland-Morris Disability
  Questionnaire at 18 weeks.
keywords:
  - Low back pain
  - Cluster randomised trial
  - Statistical analysis plan
  - Mixed models
  - Physical therapy
